WHY IT EQUALS FILM24'S.  film25 differs from film24 ONLY in the world
underneath it: assembly15 instead of assembly14.  assembly15 is assembly14's
object graph plus ground cover in TER/VEG (+17.16 % traced triangles), and
carries no lamp.  The showroom, its strip and its levelling are built by
tools/build_film_scene.py, which is byte-identical for both films.  So the
prediction is the same NUMBER arrived at by the same arithmetic -- it is not
film24's dict reused, and film_bar gets its own FILM25 literal so that
editing one film's record can never rewrite another's.

ground cover check: if assembly15 HAD added an emitter, 46203.313 (the
pre-strip interior baseline inside world/showroom_strip.py) would be wrong
and this dict would have to be re-derived rather than copied.  It is
asserted by the bar, not assumed here.
